 @Winnetou17  That may be somewhat true, but the fact remains that racing games have to render a lot of assets at break-neck speeds, and the cars themselves are expected to be rendered at a very high fidelity. So they are demanding in their own particular way.

But what's more is that what I said about Forza Horizon 4 (and we can throw DiRT Rally 2.0 into the mix as well) can just as easily be said of World War Z. These developers are taking care to optimize their games to run beautifully on all hardware, and that is a trend—hardware agnosticism—that needs to catch tf on across the industry.

(And I would especially like to know what Playground Games and Turn 10 Studios are doing in particular to get the results they do.)

